WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
- But speaking of acting,

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.410
so I asked your brother
this once, but you and...

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.810
You and he were in one of the
Harry Potter movies, right?

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:07.920
- That is correct.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.850
We were in the first one.
- Just so you know,

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.410
there will never be anything you do

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.960
that is cooler than this to me.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.510
I'm like, I think this is
the coolest thing ever.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.490
- You are not alone.
- That is crazy.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.323
- The coolest thing.

00:00:18.323 --> 00:00:20.850
- That would be my claim
to fame till I died.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.290
Like, I love Harry Potter.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.123
I love the whole...

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.020
I read all the books and
then I saw all the movies.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.160
I love the whole world.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:26.993
I think it's so creative.
- Same thing.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.004
I had just read all of the books.

00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:31.320
And then like, I was
going to school in London

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.760
at a performing arts school.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.200
And they came to our school

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.170
and were like, "We're doing this movie,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.640
but we can't tell you what it is."

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.960
We all auditioned and stuff.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.490
And then they told us
it was "Harry Potter."

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.420
And I remember...

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.620
I clearly was American

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.890
because I was like, "Can
I audition for Hermoin?

00:00:48.761 --> 00:00:51.180
- Hermoin? It's Hermione.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.050
Very American.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.850
I heard that you had a
crush on Daniel Radcliffe.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.200
Is that true?
- Oh, for sure.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.070
I was 11.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.140
We were in Gloucestershire
shooting a scene

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.430
and it was Valentine's Day.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.340
And I actually got him a beanie
baby and tried to like...

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.510
It was Valentino.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.500
Wrote him a love note.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.750
Don't know if he ever got it.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.190
I think I've told this
story a couple times

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.800
but in fact, I actually saw
Emma Watson the other day

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.080
and I walked up to her
and I was like, "Hey.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.060
We've met a few times but I
don't know if you know this,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:15.893
I was in Harry Potter."

00:01:15.893 --> 00:01:17.040
She's like, "I remember you."

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.010
I was like, "You absolutely
don't remember me."

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:20.843
I was in extra.

00:01:20.843 --> 00:01:22.680
- Maybe she's got one of those memories.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.030
- She was being kind.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:24.930
- I will say though,

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.670
you're one of those striking people though

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.890
and it's a lot to do
with your eyes, ma'am.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.050
So once you meet you,
your eyes just stand out,

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.220
especially when you're that blonde.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.300
So it's like, I don't know.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.230
She might've remembered.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.250
You're very striking.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.266
- You're very kind, too.

00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:37.470
- Just saying.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.453
No, I'm just saying,

00:01:38.453 --> 00:01:40.887
you remember somethings sometimes.

